n cubed t.

3
00:00:04,866 --> 00:00:08,041
Together, we built Chrimata, a financial
due diligence

4
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:11,216
workspace that ties each claim to its
source

5
00:00:11,216 --> 00:00:14,391
documents, captures why an analyst made a
decision,

6
00:00:14,391 --> 00:00:17,566
and brings that reasoning into the next
review.

7
00:00:17,566 --> 00:00:20,344
The question that drove us was simple:

8
00:00:20,344 --> 00:00:23,519
when new evidence changes a number, can an

9
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:26,694
agent explain what changed without
forgetting why the

10
00:00:26,694 --> 00:00:28,679
team made its earlier call?

11
00:00:28,679 --> 00:00:31,060
Let’s show you how it works.

12
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,724
Every deal has a story.

13
00:00:33,724 --> 00:00:35,993
And every decision leaves a trail.

14
00:00:36,483 --> 00:00:37,433
Meet Chrimata.

15
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:41,230
Due diligence rebuilt around the evidence,
the context,

16
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:43,603
and every decision that follows.

17
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,713
All right, let's step inside.

18
00:00:47,783 --> 00:00:51,463
And here, every live mandate—clear at a
glance.

19
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:54,923
And from there, the review queue links
each

20
00:00:54,923 --> 00:00:57,013
open question to the evidence behind it.

21
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:01,981
So, follow a claim back to its source.

22
00:01:01,981 --> 00:01:05,329
One click brings up the document, the
exact

23
00:01:05,329 --> 00:01:06,584
page, the evidence.

24
00:01:06,584 --> 00:01:08,676
No more hunting through folders.

25
00:01:08,676 --> 00:01:09,513
No guesswork.

26
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:13,141
And now, new evidence lands.

27
00:01:13,141 --> 00:01:16,513
See what changed, and which findings it
touches.

28
00:01:16,513 --> 00:01:19,886
Your team can keep moving without starting
the

29
00:01:19,886 --> 00:01:20,729
review over.

30
00:01:20,729 --> 00:01:21,993
No lost context.

31
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:28,013
And then there’s Hindsight.

32
00:01:28,013 --> 00:01:31,373
It remembers why decisions were made, not
just

33
00:01:31,373 --> 00:01:31,793
what.

34
00:01:31,793 --> 00:01:35,153
So when a familiar issue returns, the
reasoning

35
00:01:35,153 --> 00:01:38,093
is already there, when it matters most.

36
00:01:39,083 --> 00:01:40,903
Here’s the failure mode.

37
00:01:40,903 --> 00:01:44,543
New evidence changes MRR, but it doesn’t
automatically

38
00:01:44,543 --> 00:01:46,818
invalidate the analyst’s earlier
explanation.

39
00:01:46,818 --> 00:01:50,458
Without memory, the agent sees the latest
numbers

40
00:01:50,458 --> 00:01:54,098
and open questions, but not why a related

41
00:01:54,098 --> 00:01:55,463
issue was resolved.

42
00:01:55,463 --> 00:01:59,103
It can reopen the same work or ask

43
00:01:59,103 --> 00:02:01,378
for the same evidence again.

44
00:02:01,378 --> 00:02:05,018
Chrimata runs that review twice—first
without memory, then

45
00:02:05,018 --> 00:02:08,203
with Hindsight—so we can compare the
results.

46
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:17,090
And when it’s time to ask a question,

47
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:18,980
just ask in plain language.

48
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:22,003
Chrimata brings in the history, the
evidence, the

49
00:02:22,003 --> 00:02:25,027
context—so your answer actually moves the
work forward.

50
00:02:26,017 --> 00:02:28,657
Every answer, grounded in the source.

51
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:36,418
Here’s the flow.

52
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:40,022
The interface sends an analyst’s decision
through the

53
00:02:40,022 --> 00:02:43,627
API gateway—over REST, or as a live
stream.

54
00:02:43,627 --> 00:02:47,231
The gateway routes review pipelines for
change reviews

55
00:02:47,231 --> 00:02:50,835
and evidence requests, or sends questions
to the

56
00:02:50,835 --> 00:02:51,736
Ask agent.

57
00:02:51,736 --> 00:02:54,439
PostgreSQL tracks each ticket and status.

58
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:58,044
Hindsight retains the decision and
reasoning, then recalls

59
00:02:58,044 --> 00:03:00,747
past outcomes when similar issues return.

60
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,653
What surprised me is that the hardest part

61
00:03:08,653 --> 00:03:10,748
isn’t finding the new number;

62
00:03:10,748 --> 00:03:14,101
it’s remembering why the team treated it
that

63
00:03:14,101 --> 00:03:14,520
way.

64
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,873
Hindsight brings back the earlier decision
and explanation,

65
00:03:17,873 --> 00:03:20,388
while PostgreSQL tracks current ticket
state.

66
00:03:20,388 --> 00:03:23,741
The agent still checks today’s evidence,
and a

67
00:03:23,741 --> 00:03:26,255
real contradiction can change the outcome.

68
00:03:26,255 --> 00:03:28,770
Memory doesn’t make a decision permanent;

69
00:03:28,770 --> 00:03:32,123
it gives the next review enough context to

70
00:03:32,123 --> 00:03:33,380
question it intelligently.

71
00:03:35,058 --> 00:03:35,658
Chrimata.

72
00:03:35,658 --> 00:03:39,858
Due diligence, rebuilt for the
intelligence era.
